## canonical HEAD comparison

Command:

```bash
./node_modules/node/bin/node -e "const cp=require('node:child_process'); const head=JSON.parse(cp.execFileSync('git',['show','HEAD:policy/routing.json'],{encoding:'utf8'})); const work=require('./policy/routing.json'); delete work.classification; if(JSON.stringify(head)!==JSON.stringify(work)) process.exit(1); console.log('canonical-head-compare:passed')"
```

Exit code: 0

Output:

```text
canonical-head-compare:passed
```

## Harness note

An earlier, non-recorded canonical-comparison harness invocation passed a string where Node required an options object and exited 1 before reading the HEAD document. The corrected command above uses `{encoding:'utf8'}` and passed. This was a harness error, not a repository verification failure.
